# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — Company Standard Template
# Based on GitLab Server Security Policy — Blocked files and folders are listed here.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⚠️ FACING ISSUES WHILE PUSHING TO GIT? (PUSH REJECTED)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If you are encountering push rejection errors or security policy violations,
# download and apply this company standard .gitignore template directly into your
# project root to prevent tracking blocked files (e.g., .env, credentials,
# node_modules, build outputs, debug logs, private keys, etc.).
#
# Quick Download Commands (run from your project root):
#
#   Using curl:
#   curl -sL https://webhook.devtechnosys.tech/git/scripts/gitignore_template/ -o .gitignore
#   # Or via short URL alias:
#   curl -sL https://webhook.devtechnosys.tech/git/gitignore/ -o .gitignore
#
#   Using wget:
#   wget https://webhook.devtechnosys.tech/git/scripts/gitignore_template/ -O .gitignore
#   # Or via short URL alias:
#   wget https://webhook.devtechnosys.tech/git/gitignore/ -O .gitignore
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# QUICK FIX: IF BLOCKED FILES ARE ALREADY COMMITTED / TRACKED:
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Untrack the blocked file(s) from Git index without deleting local files:
#    git rm -r --cached <file_or_folder>
#    (Example: git rm --cached .env  OR  git rm -r --cached node_modules/)
#
# 2. Stage and commit the .gitignore:
#    git add .gitignore
#    git commit -m "chore: apply standard .gitignore and untrack blocked files"
#
# 3. Push to GitLab:
#    git push
#
# Last Updated: August 2026
# =============================================================================


# =============================================================================
# [1] ENVIRONMENT & SECRETS  ← MOST IMPORTANT
# =============================================================================

# Environment files (NEVER push these)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.development
.env.staging
.env.production
.env.test
.env.backup
.env.*

# Allow example / template environment files (Safe to commit)
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template

# Certificate & Key files
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.cer
*.crt
*.der
*.mobileprovision

# Credential files
credentials.json
secret.json
secrets.json
*.secret
auth.json

# SSH Private Keys
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519

# Java / Android Keystores
*.keystore
*.jks


# =============================================================================
# [2] IDE & SYSTEM FILES
# =============================================================================

# macOS
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Windows
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# VS Code
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# JetBrains IDEs (IntelliJ, PhpStorm, WebStorm, PyCharm, Android Studio)
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr

# Visual Studio
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?


# =============================================================================
